  "solution": "**Given:**\n\nx + y = 65\n\nsqrt{xy} = 26\n\n**Formula used:**\n\n(1)/(x) + (1)/(y) = (x + y)/(xy)\n\n**Calculations:**\n\n⇒ sqrt{xy} = 26\n\n⇒ xy = 26²\n\n⇒ xy = 676\n\n⇒ (1)/(x) + (1)/(y) = (65)/(676)\n\n⇒ (1)/(x) + (1)/(y) = (5 times 13)/(52 times 13)\n\n⇒ (1)/(x) + (1)/(y) = (5)/(52)\n\n**∴ The correct answer is option (1).**",
